The '''TIE/vn space superiority fighter''',<ref name="TLJ:ICS" /> formally known as the '''TIE vendetta space superiority fighter'''<ref name="TFOWM" /> and nicknamed the '''TIE silencer''', was an angular variant of the [[TIE series|TIE fighter series]] [[starfighter]]s used by the [[First Order]]. A product of [[Sienar-Jaemus Fleet Systems]], its aggressive design and equally impressive firepower was specifically crafted for use among the most elite members of the First Order.<ref name="Sienar-Jaemus Analyst">{{FFGXW|set=TIE Silencer Expansion Pack|cardname=First Order Test Pilot}}</ref> As such, the fighter was [[engineer]]ed for speed and handling, though lesser [[pilot]]s were still often overwhelmed and unable to maintain control of the nimble [[Starship|ship]].<ref name="FFG">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/news/2017/9/8/finish-what-you-start|text=Finish What You Start}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
{{Quote|I can't believe how quiet she runs. And how cool. Any other ship'd be burning up hot.|Dec Hansen|<ref name="Attack on Starkiller Base" />}}
[[File:TIE_Silencer_cockpit.png|thumb|left|250px|The cockpit of the TIE silencer]]
As an advanced prototype starfighter, the TIE/vn incorporated the latest First Order military innovations, including experimental stealth gear meant to foil sensors and tracking. It featured a [[hyperdrive]] and a [[deflector shield generator]] and projector, and was powered by a starboard reactor. Twin ion thrust arrays at the rear of the ship acted as its engines. Along its wings were [[solar collector]] arrays, which featured a corrugated surface to maximize energy absorption. The ship featured a flight computer and could be modified to include customized flight controls for a single pilot, who entered the ship through a cabin access hatch at the top of the vessel.<ref name="TLJ:ICS" />

Working at hidden Sienar-Jaemus facilities, First Order designers reconfigured the weapons package of the [[TIE/sf space superiority fighter|TIE/sf]] to incorporate advances in power storage and energy conversion. For the TIE/vn, the TIE/sf's power cell spokes were replaced by a next-generation array protected beneath the hull, with shorter runs for trunk lines and converter coils. Rather than replicate the TIE/sf's ventral turret, the silencer relocated its missiles and heavy cannons to the wing apertures, giving the pilot superior targeting and a wider field of fire. Targeting sensors were also located in the wing aperture. Laser bolts were contained in a magnetic field bubble.<ref name="TLJ:ICS" />

==History==
{{Quote|Oh, my gosh, a silencer!|[[Cost Niktur]]|<ref name="Attack on Starkiller Base" />}}
<div style="float:right">[[File:TIE_Silencer_firing.png|thumb|left|250px|A TIE silencer firing its laser cannons]]</div>
The pedigree of the TIE silencer traced back to the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[TIE/d "Defender" Multi-Role Starfighter]], a hybrid fighter-[[bomber]] that never saw widespread use in the Galactic Civil War. The ship was revived by First Order technicians who saw it as a versatile attack craft to throw at New Republic forces. The [[TIE/sf space superiority fighter]] was an early attempt to bring heavier weapons to the battlefield along with the next-generation power capabilities needed to support them&mdash;improvements later incorporated into the silencer.<ref name="TLJ:ICS" /> It featured other design similarities to the Empire's [[TIE/IN interceptor]] and [[TIE Advanced x1]].<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|tie-silencer|TIE silencer}}</ref>

The TIE/vn was test piloted by an ill-fated individual codenamed "[["Blackout"]], who flew the starfighter and fired its weaponry in a volcanic area.<ref name="X-Wing">{{FFGXW2|set=First Order Conversion Kit|cardname="Blackout"|reprint=1}}</ref> [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] also utilized [[Kylo Ren's TIE silencer|his own TIE silencer]]. His detailed post-flight reports allowed Sienar-Jaemus techs to refine the onboard systems, with an eye towards the day when shipyards were to begin mass-producing silencers for the regime's frontline units.<ref name="TLJ:ICS" /> [[Klimo]], a [[Resistance pilot]] who was a member of [[J-Squadron]], hijacked a TIE silencer just as it was getting primed for refueling. It was then used to aid J-Squadron in getting into [[Starkiller Base]], which was shortly thereafter destroyed in a [[Battle of Starkiller Base|Resistance attack]].<ref name="Attack on Starkiller Base" />

[[File:MagPulseWarheadCanon.png|thumb|left|250px|The silencer's starboard torpedo launcher]]
Shortly after the loss of Starkiller Base but with the Resistance on the run, Ren flew his silencer in the [[Battle of Oetchi]] at the head of<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref> his [[Kylo Ren's personal squadron|personal TIE squadron]].<ref name="TLJ:TVD">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> Upon sensing his mother, [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], aboard the Resistance flagship ''[[Raddus (MC85 Star Cruiser)|Raddus]]'', Ren found himself unable to fire upon the enemy vessel, only for his wingmen to complete the attack run and destroy the [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]]. All the same, Organa was able to use [[the Force]] to pull herself to safety upon being sucked into [[Realspace|space]].<ref name="Episode VIII" /> Ren continued to use his TIE/vn during his reign as [[Supreme Leader]]<ref name="Rise of Resistance">{{GEAttr|Star Wars: Rise of the Resistance}}</ref> but also utilized a [[Kylo Ren's TIE whisper|TIE whisper]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:TIE_Silencer_Fathead.png|thumb|right|250px|The TIE silencer from multiple angles]]
The TIE/vn [[Realspace|space]] superiority fighter was created and developed for [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']],<ref name="SW Show">{{StarWarsShow|tMTExpDs7WA|Kylo Ren's New Ship, The Last Jedi Cast at D23, & Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge!|sw_url=video/kylo-ren-s-new-ship-the-last-jedi-cast-at-d23-and-star-wars-galaxy-s-edge}}</ref> the eighth film in the ''[[Star Wars]]'' saga, which was released on [[December 15]], [[2017]].<ref name="The Last Jedi">{{SW|url=news/the-official-title-for-star-wars-episode-viii-revealed|text=The Official Title for ''Star Wars: Episode VIII'' Revealed}}</ref> The [[Starship|ship]] was officially revealed on ''[[The Star Wars Show]]'' on [[July 19]], 2017.<ref name="SW Show date">{{StarWarsShow|tMTExpDs7WA|Kylo Ren's New Ship, The Last Jedi Cast at D23, & Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge!|sw_url=video/kylo-ren-s-new-ship-the-last-jedi-cast-at-d23-and-star-wars-galaxy-s-edge}}</ref> The TIE silencer was named by the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]]'s [[Pablo Hidalgo]]. Although Hidalgo considered the name "TIE vendetta," he eventually decided on "TIE silencer," but hinted at the old name ("/vn") in the full technical name.<ref name="Hidalgo tweet">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/894419876567105536|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=At one point it was gonna be called a TIE vendetta. But went with silencer instead, but kept the /vn. That's the real-world answer, anyway.|archivefile=File:TIEvn.png}}</ref>

The TIE silencer first appeared in the [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]'' on [[November 9]], 2017.<ref name="GoH">{{WebCite|url=https://swgohevents.com/event/first-order-relentless-iii|text=The First Order Relentless III|work=SWGOH Events|archivedate=20201227132052}}</ref>

